cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus or code, please cite the paper below."
title: "YouTube Safe Kids — toxicity filter: corpus and code"
abstract: >-
  Annotated corpus of 1,811 Brazilian Portuguese sentences transcribed from 206
  public YouTube videos, labelled by three raters into three toxicity levels,
  together with the annotation guideline, the video-disjoint split, the training
  and evaluation code of a BERTimbau classifier and the prototype that reranks
  children's video search results by an interpretable verbal-toxicity score.
type: dataset
# Terms differ by component -- see LICENSE. MIT covers the code; the annotation
# is CC BY 4.0; the transcribed sentences are third-party material quoted for
# research, over which no licence is granted. CFF admits a single value, so the
# one naming the code is given here and LICENSE is authoritative.
license: MIT
